    "evidence": "When the containment pit was drained, a relatively small quantity of NaHS27 reacted with acid in the sewer to produce H2S. The H2S leaked through a faulty manway cover seal into the area where the contractors were working.",
    "explanation": "The incident involved the generation and release of hydrogen sulfide (H2S), a highly toxic gas, which dispersed from the sewer system into the work area, exposing and harming workers."
  },
  {
    "name": "Asphyxiation",
    "evidence": "When the containment pit was drained, a relatively small quantity of NaHS27 reacted with acid in the sewer to produce H2S. The H2S leaked through a faulty manway cover seal into the area where the contractors were working. ... two workers were killed and eight injured while performing maintenance near a NaHS transfer terminal.",
    "explanation": "The release of H2S gas into the work area led to fatalities and injuries, consistent with asphyxiation due to exposure to a toxic atmosphere that displaces oxygen or interferes with respiration."
  }
]

